Usage:
  nucleus new <project_name> [flags]

Create a new project scaffold: go.mod pinned to this release, a composition-root main.go, nucleus.yml and an empty migrations directory. No feature code is generated.

Arguments:
  <project_name>  Directory created under --out; also the default module path suffix (example.com/<project_name>)

Templates (--template):
  mvc  Full-stack: default subsystems, rbac_policy.csv and the sqlite driver import (default)
  api  Core-only: WithoutDefaults(), no admin, storage, mail or authz

Flags:
  -force
    	Overwrite scaffold files if the project directory exists
  -module string
    	Go module path (default: example.com/<project_name>)
  -out string
    	Parent directory where the project folder will be created (default ".")
  -port int
    	HTTP port in nucleus.yml (default 8080)
  -template string
    	Starter template (mvc: full-stack, api: lightweight core-only) (default "mvc")

Examples:
  nucleus new blog --module github.com/acme/blog
  nucleus new svc --template api --port 9090
